[description]

This package provides a widget to show the information of a single [term geo/box] definition.

[para] The widget shows a table with the corners of the box, its center, as latitude and
longitude, and its diameter and perimeter. Distances are formatted for display with
[cmd {map slippy pretty-distance}] of package [package map::slippy].

[section API]

[list_begin definitions]
[call [cmd ::map::box::display] [arg pathName]]

Creates a new box display widget [arg pathName]. The widget has no options. The result of the
command is [arg pathName]. The command is also available as [cmd {map box display}].

[para] The widget initially shows nothing. Use method [method set] to show a box.

[list_end]

The widget supports the following method:

[list_begin definitions]
[call [arg pathName] [method set] [arg geobox]]

Shows the box specified by [arg geobox], a list of four numbers, the minimal latitude, minimal
longitude, maximal latitude, and maximal longitude, in this order. This is the [const geo] element
of a [term geo/box] value as described in [package map::box::file]. An empty list clears the
display.

[para] The result of the method is the empty string.

[list_end]

[section EXAMPLE]

[example {
package require map::box::display

map box display .box
pack .box -fill both -expand 1

.box set {48.0 11.0 48.1 11.2}
}]

